WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.170
<i>The spring when I started middle school</i>

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.010
<i>was when I got used to walking alone.</i>

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.330
Hello.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.790
Oh, Nodoka-chan! It's been a while.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.570
Where's Shizuno-chan?

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.960
We've kind of drifted apart 
since starting middle school.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.380
Well, there are times when that happens.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.330
Yes.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.890
<i>Like going to a new school,</i>

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:43.480
<i>changing classes, changing schools...</i>

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:44.980
<i>Chi!</i>

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.590
<i>Everyone drifts away, bit by bit.</i>

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.480
<i>If I knew it would feel like this,</i>

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.960
<i>I never would've...</i>

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.040
Next Year

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.040
Spring of 2nd Year of Middle School

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.040
Sorry!

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.780
They're so big, I couldn't get past... hey...

00:01:25.910 --> 00:01:27.340
Are you okay?

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.630
Is this like one of those 
things where a glancing blow

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:31.320
against the chin scrambles 
your opponent's brains?!

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.280
You just threw me off balance.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.870
Is your brain okay?

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.200
I could ask you the same thing.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.450
Huh?

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.660
I was just thinking that 
you remind me a tiny bit

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.960
of two friends I had back in grade school.

00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:57.670
Hey, that means we can be friends, too!

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.530
You're right.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.150
Two Months Later

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.150
Takatoobara 
Middle School

00:02:14.150 --> 00:02:16.150
<b>Mahjong Club</b>

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:19.080
Welcome to the Takatoobara 
Middle School Mahjong Club!

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:22.190
Nice to meet ya!

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:23.910
It's nice to meet you.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.880
It's nice to meet you, too.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.000
Yes! It's so marvelous that 
our club has two new members!

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.290
It's super marvelous!

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.090
Now we can enter team tournaments.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:35.110
I don't know about that.

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:36.570
I mean, I'm a third year,

00:02:36.570 --> 00:02:38.720
and next year, I'll be going 
to a school in Fukuoka.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:40.640
Plus, the prefectural preliminaries

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.110
for this year's inter-middle 
are already over.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:43.180
Oh, yeah.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:49.260
I wish I had known you 
were into mahjong earlier.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.210
Huh? I'm sorry.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:54.360
It's still marvelous!

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.530
If you guys get another member next year,

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.820
you can enter the inter-middle!

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:02.110
I'll be praying for your success from 
all the way out in Kyuushuu!

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.340
You're jumping the gun...

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.200
What about that girl?

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.370
That childhood friend of Muro's who

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.160
usually picks her up at the school gate.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:09.960
She's in grade school.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.840
E-Excuse me!

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.240
I'm Yumeno Maho.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.720
It's nice to meet you.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:26.840
Marvelous!

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.480
Welcome to the Takatoobara 
Middle School Mahjong Club!

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:30.950
We're glad you came!

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.460
<i>Shizuno... Ako...</i>

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:37.230
<i>Even knowing I'll have to 
part with them someday,</i>

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.990
<i>friends are fun to have, so I'm happy.</i>

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.220
<i>I hope we meet again...</i>

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:46.980
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.540
July 
Joint Training Camp

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:52.920
<b>Hand 3: 
Start</b>

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.420
Dealer: Maho

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.420
East Hand 1
Bonus 1

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:05.290
Ugh, now we gotta deal with Mahocchi.

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.760
Mahocchi?

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.890
She started playing mahjong 
online thanks to your influence.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:15.770
She plays as this angel 
called "Super Mahocchi."

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.310
But she's really weak. 
Her rating is in the 1200s.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:23.110
1200?

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.070
Riichi!

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:42.260
No-ten.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.290
Tenpai.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.780
<i>She bailed out really cleanly, 
just like Nodoka.</i>

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.920
I guess you can't copy this part of her!

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.170
<i>Her play history shows 
that for one hand each game,</i>

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:54.060
<i>she plays just like Nodoka or Yuuki.</i>

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:54.410
Bye!

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.560
Sheesh...

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.940
<i>Is she a girl who can only utilize 
what she's learned for one hand...</i>

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.650
East Hand 2

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.650
Carried Bonus 2

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:02.690
<i>Or is it...</i>

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:06.790
<i>If I discard the dora 3 of circles I just got,</i>

00:05:06.790 --> 00:05:08.670
<i>it looks like I could have a three-sided wait...</i>

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.540
<i>I feel like this dora is 
here for a reason, though.</i>

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:19.290
Ron!

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:22.460
With the two bonus counters, that's 8,600.

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:23.510
Yes.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.420
<i>Hmm...</i>

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.260
East Hand 3

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.510
Huh?

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.680
Are you maybe waiting 
for the 5 of characters?

00:05:37.880 --> 00:05:41.440
I feel like I can win with a dead wall draw.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.690
Kan!

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:54.830
Rinshan kaihou, tsumo, two dora.

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:59.330
That's 2,000 and 4,000.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:07.220
<i>She's the real deal.</i>

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:11.970
<i>Rinshan kaihou...</i>

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:15.340
<i>Who is this girl?</i>

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:17.230
I did it!

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:21.230
<i>Miyanaga-san?</i>

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.690
East Hand 4

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.760
Turn #11

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:31.910
Kan on that!

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.620
<i>Huh, again?</i>

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:38.620
Rinshan...

00:06:43.660 --> 00:06:45.370
Tsumo, it is not.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:53.130
Th-This hand...

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:58.990
has no yaku at all anymore!

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:02.640
You don't really have to announce that.

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:07.170
Ron.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.590
12,000.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:15.110
I thought I taught you to not take cheap kans.

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:16.330
B-But...

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:19.430
Miyanaga-senpai's

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:22.460
rinshan kaihou win in the prefectural 
preliminaries was so amazing,

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:25.400
and whenever you're around,

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:30.510
I can't get it out of my head 
and want to play like that, too.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.590
It didn't work this time,

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:39.720
but last hand, I actually felt 
like, maybe, I could do it.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:42.230
That kind of superstition doesn't happen.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.390
You've always played like that.

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:48.560
You'd imitate Yuuki's or my play style,

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.990
and it'd maybe work for one hand each day.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:56.010
<i>She looks up to them so much, 
she can't help emulating them?</i>

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:00.580
You should improve your own base 
skills before imitating others.

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:06.830
Hey, Maho's giving it her best.

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.320
She goes to lessons run by pros,

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.460
and she practices at the club until late every day.

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:14.590
I was too harsh.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:18.600
It's been four months since then.
Let's see how much you've grown.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:20.850
This is just the beginning, after all.

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.060
Yes!

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.560
South Hand 1

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:26.610
<i>I'm the dealer.</i>

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.920
<i>I'm going to give it my best!</i>

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:34.030
Maho, you'll have too many 
tiles if you draw now!

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.470
Oh, yeah...

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:40.120
You can't get through a day 
without at least one mistake.

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.650
Even though she's been 
playing for over a year?

00:08:42.650 --> 00:08:44.950
She's an eternal newbie!

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.810
I see.

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:48.330
Right?

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:53.160
A joint training camp?

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:54.620
That's right.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.890
I'd like to bring four schools 
together for a training camp.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:08:59.350
Why don't you do it, Yasuko?

00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:03.480
Is there a secret reason why 
you don't want a pro involved?

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:05.390
The World Junior Championships?

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:09.290
Or a candidate for this fall's nationals?

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:14.520
So you're looking for players you wouldn't
find at normal qualifying competitions.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:17.940
Am I not included in that group?

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:19.500
I wonder...

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.100
Not that it matters.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:22.380
Huh?

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:23.950
Never mind.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:27.640
Don't talk to me so casually at the camp.

00:09:27.640 --> 00:09:29.750
I've got to keep up my dignity as a pro.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.150
Huh?

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:33.570
I thought that had crumbled ages ago.

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:34.800
What?!

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.030
You don't have to tell me. 
I'll watch what I say.

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:40.000
Please do that.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.130
Seriously.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:46.180
Scores

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:46.180
Maho   |   Muro   |   Nodoka   |   Saki

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:47.830
I guess you came in last in all three 
East-South matches, Maho.

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:49.900
That's our No-Good Maho.

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.690
I tried, but I guess it wasn't good enough.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.800
<i>Whatever Yasuko's motivations are,</i>

00:09:55.800 --> 00:09:58.640
<i>I'm doing this training camp for Kiyosumi,</i>

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.600
<i>in order to reduce our team's 
anxiety for Nationals!</i>

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:05.100
<i>First things first: making Mako stronger.</i>

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.200
<i>Mako can remember the layout of the table</i>

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:11.080
<i>in the same way she'd remember someone's face.</i>

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.330
<i>However, thanks to Tsuruga's Senoo-san,</i>

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:17.470
<i>I've seen that we need 
to expand her repertoire.</i>

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:22.880
<i>The main point of this camp 
will be to give Mako more data.</i>

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:25.720
<i>Plus, we're adding a special 
newcomer to the mix.</i>

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:29.370
<i>I wasn't so sure Senoo-san alone was enough...</i>

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:35.110
<i>But this will vastly expand Mako's repertoire!</i>

00:10:35.540 --> 00:10:36.640
<i>Moreover,</i>

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:40.550
<i>since the prefectural preliminaries,
Saki's been a bit unsteady on her feet.</i>

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:44.120
<i>I was hoping she'd be more 
focused going into the Nationals,</i>

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:49.320
<i>but right now, even if a strong challenger 
appears, Saki just gets excited.</i>

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:50.860
<i>So then...</i>

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:54.750
<i>People are afraid of that which 
encroaches on their territory.</i>

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:00.010
<i>It looks like her magic has worked a bit.</i>

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:06.280
<i>Even if Nodoka and Yuuki will get stronger</i>

00:11:06.280 --> 00:11:07.940
<i>as we face off against other schools,</i>

00:11:07.940 --> 00:11:10.730
<i>we'll still need something 
else for them as well.</i>

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.060
I'm stepping out for a bit.

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:16.230
<i>As for myself...</i>

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:18.440
<b>Ryuumonbuchi 
High School
Team</b>

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:18.440
Hello!

00:11:18.750 --> 00:11:20.110
We have a visitor!

00:11:20.770 --> 00:11:22.380
Welcome.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:25.330
What can we do for you?

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:27.220
<i>Nothing's changed here.</i>

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:28.400
<i>That's too bad.</i>

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:31.580
I wanted to play 
mahjong with Amae-san.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:34.040
Really?!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:35.090
You betcha!

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:40.470
<b>Tsuruga Academy
Team</b>

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:39.080
Yumi!

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:40.470
I'm counting on you again today.

00:11:40.900 --> 00:11:43.800
H-H-How come you're calling 
her by her first name?

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:46.520
We became close last night.

00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:48.890
Last night... close?!

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:52.480
Calm down, Momo. It's not like 
something special's going on.

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:57.320
What do you mean by "something"?!

00:12:12.950 --> 00:12:14.210
Looking forward to it.

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:16.540
Sure.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:23.070
Did you pack everything?

00:12:23.070 --> 00:12:24.990
Yes, we got everything.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:25.890
Then let's go.

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:30.640
If we leave now, we can get 
back to Tsuruga by nine.

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:37.370
You go ahead.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.710
Yesterday's goodbyes 
should have been enough.

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:46.620
Last night's game was so exciting, 
I couldn't really sleep.

00:12:47.520 --> 00:12:49.870
Send-offs aren't really your thing, are they?

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:53.120
Thank you.

00:12:53.530 --> 00:12:56.640
I really appreciate you coming.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:59.710
Have you always been so sentimental?

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.470
I guess that's not really me.

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:04.410
I'm grateful, too.

00:13:05.180 --> 00:13:07.910
I might be lacking real competitive spirit.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.540
Losing in the prefectural preliminaries

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:13.640
helped me to actually enjoy this camp.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.570
But having fun is probably 
not enough for you guys.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:21.780
There's something else waiting for you.

00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:24.090
This summer might be

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:27.410
the first time I sincerely 
cheer for another school.

00:13:31.850 --> 00:13:33.160
Um...

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:37.970
I made some lunch boxes in 
between making breakfast.

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:39.880
You can take one if you like.

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:44.240
Take care.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:44.920
Thanks.

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:50.510
Kazekoshi's captain!

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.110
Can you please give this to Bundou-san?

00:13:59.110 --> 00:14:00.520
A card?

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:04.400
Let's meet again.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.840
Wahaha.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:22.120
In a moment, the seventh through ninth

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:25.420
of the inter-high's first round matches will begin.

00:14:32.970 --> 00:14:34.140
Kan!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.960
Rinshan...

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.100
kaihou, it is not.

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:43.430
It's the third players' match of 
the ninth first round match!

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:45.860
Things have gotten interesting!

00:14:46.370 --> 00:14:48.950
Currently in the lead is Karouto High School,
representing Hiroshima.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:50.930
Karoutou High School
 (Hiroshima)
 3rd Year
 Sasano Ichigo

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.320
They're keeping up the overwhelming lead

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.870
they built up in the first players' match.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.480
Fifth in the spring tournament,

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:58.870
Himematsu High School is 50,000 
points behind and trying to catch up!

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:58.870
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 3rd Year
 Atago Hiroe

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:02.880
Hida Business School 
(Gifu)
 2nd Year
 Fushiya Natsu

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:02.880
Kuratsuki High School 
(Ishikawa)
 2nd Year
 Noguchi Ayaka

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:01.200
How will Hida Business School 
and Kuratsuki High School

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:02.880
make their move?!

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:05.750
<i>Gifu's in third place.</i>

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:09.390
<i>The dealer, Hida Business 
School, declared riichi.</i>

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:11.430
<i>In response,</i>

00:15:11.430 --> 00:15:13.260
<i>Himematsu called kan, adding to their pon.</i>

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:17.140
<i>And then she said "kaihou, it is not."
 Is she even in tenpai?</i>

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:20.390
<i>Kuratsuki was out on the first turn.</i>

00:15:20.390 --> 00:15:22.320
<i>Let's see.</i>

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:25.480
<i>If I win on a draw, I'll get a sanbaiman, 
even without declaring riichi.</i>

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:29.400
<i>The 9 of bamboo is safe since it was 
discarded by Kuratsuki and the dealer,</i>

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:32.220
<i>but Himematsu could be going 
for a chanta or a toitoi.</i>

00:15:32.220 --> 00:15:33.700
<i>The 8 of bamboo is visible,</i>

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.410
<i>so if they're waiting for a 
9 of bamboo, it's a hell wait.</i>

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.080
<i>If that's the case,</i>

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:40.250
<i>they would have changed their wait 
to the 1 of characters that they</i>

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.920
<i>drew from the dead wall.</i>

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:44.130
<i>So my move's gotta be...</i>

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:45.420
<i>How do you like this?</i>

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.000
Ron.

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:50.050
<i>I dealt right into it...</i>

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:54.050
<i>I guess it's good that I was able 
to rotate the dealer cheaply.</i>

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:58.310
I normally think chantas are too cheap,

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:02.350
but this time, I must say I'm glad they are.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.290
<i>She made a kan of the 9 of circles,</i>

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:08.320
<i>but didn't make a kan with 
the 1 of characters!?</i>

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:10.320
<i>Which means this hand is...</i>

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:11.320
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.070
<i>Chinroutou?!</i>

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:14.070
[Chinroutou: A yakuman hand made of only 1s and 9s]

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:16.810
32,000.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:19.330
Hurts more than ya thought, huh?

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:26.330
I hadn't taken that into consideration...

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:29.880
The third players' match of the 
ninth first round match is over!

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.360
Himematsu High School's captain,

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:36.010
Atago Hiroe, turns the tables 
with a direct yakuman hit!

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.130
The winner!

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:40.970
<i>It's my first inter-high yakuman!</i>

00:16:40.970 --> 00:16:41.620
<b>Himematsu</b>

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:41.980
<b>Himematsu</b>

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:45.970
Isn't anyone going to come get me?!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.740
Welcome back, sis!

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.770
Good game, captain.

00:16:53.770 --> 00:16:55.930
Are there other matches still going on?

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:58.320
Nagano's really amazing!

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:00.040
Nagano?

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:02.540
<i>Kiyosumi High School...</i>

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:08.830
The dealer's been on a winning 
streak with all these crazy wins.

00:17:08.830 --> 00:17:10.590
That sort of luck is ridiculous.

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:15.110
Kiyosumi, huh?

00:17:15.110 --> 00:17:17.970
They're the ones who beat Ryuumonbuchi.

00:17:18.380 --> 00:17:20.100
They're scary, huh?

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:21.850
Amae Koromo-chan.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:25.350
That tiny girl was really amazing last year.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:28.000
Last year, she singlehandedly 
bumped out two schools

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:31.800
in the first round match, 
and three schools in the second.

00:17:31.800 --> 00:17:34.880
But I bet Kiyosumi is 
even better than that.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.030
Then these three schools 
are going to be tough.

00:17:38.030 --> 00:17:38.620
Why?

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:42.730
Is it because their prefectures 
have few schools to begin with?

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:46.960
It doesn't matter what the reason is.
Don't underestimate them.

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:48.500
Princess...

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:52.410
Even if another region has 20 schools,

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:57.660
that means they won just as much 
as the team they played against

00:17:57.660 --> 00:17:59.220
at Kagoshima's finals.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.440
Among the three final schools 
in the prefectural preliminaries,

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:04.980
were there any that we could 
afford to underestimate?

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:15.450
Let's meet all of our opponents with respect.

00:18:15.450 --> 00:18:18.610
And it's over!

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.690
It's Kiyosumi High School's 
third player, Takei Hisa!

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:24.150
In bonus hand 6, she 
unleashes a direct haneman hit!

00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:28.120
They've won their first round match without 
even going to the fourth player!

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:30.530
Now this is something.

00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:34.630
I'm going to have to teach 
them a little lesson.

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:38.480
It's the fifth day of the inter-high,

00:18:38.480 --> 00:18:42.390
and we will finally see two 
of the four seeded schools!

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.890
This is where the top 16 will 
begin to be narrowed down.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:49.390
Which schools will survive 
the next two round matches?

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.510
The third players' match is off to a quiet start.

00:18:53.140 --> 00:18:56.300
Shirataki Itokonnyaku is so strong!

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.650
Shindouji and Kariyasuga are good, too.

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:04.410
<i>Saki-san, your sister's school is in that match...</i>

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.510
<i>Shouldn't you be watching?</i>

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:24.260
Next Day

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:24.260
<i>It's the sixth day of the inter-high.</i>

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:27.270
<i>Today we'll see the third and fourth 
of the second round matches!</i>

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:30.770
<i>The first players' match is about to begin.</i>

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:39.710
All right! My taco power is fully charged!

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:41.280
You're going already?

00:19:41.630 --> 00:19:42.530
Isn't it too early?

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:45.350
I'm going to touch up my makeup.

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:46.410
Good luck!

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:46.930
Yup!

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:48.950
Just like we practiced, okay?

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:50.540
Go get 'em.

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:54.790
Leave it to me!

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.050
I'm going now!

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.740
The third match, on Stage A,

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:04.050
will be the compelling match-up of 
Eisui Girls' and Himematsu High.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:07.230
Commentating the game today 
will be myself, Satou.

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:10.010
Assisting me is the up-and-coming pro, Kainou,

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:12.450
winner of last year's Newcomer Award.

00:20:12.450 --> 00:20:14.060
Good morning, it is.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.430
Thank you.

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:22.020
Pro player Kainou's alma mater, 
the Oujou Girls' Academy,

00:20:22.020 --> 00:20:24.260
competed in this year's inter-high as well,

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:27.650
but unfortunately, they were 
eliminated in the first round match.

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:30.450
It was a painfully close game.

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:33.580
Our opponents were energetic and very strong.

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:36.790
Energetic?

00:20:37.530 --> 00:20:41.280
Well, the participants in the 
first players' match are coming in!

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:44.420
Representing Kagoshima prefecture 
is the player from Eisui Girls'

00:20:44.420 --> 00:20:47.470
who was extremely successful
in last year's team tournament:

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:51.140
Jindai Komaki!

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:52.120
Eisui Girls' (Kagoshima)
 2nd Year
 Jindai Komaki

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:56.440
Representing Iwate prefecture, 
we have Miyamori Girls'.

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:59.560
Their first player is Hosegawa Shiromi.

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:01.380
Miyamori Girls'  (Iwate)
 3rd Year
 Hosegawa Shiromi

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.480
I'm so tired.

00:21:02.920 --> 00:21:06.740
From Himematsu High School of South Osaka,
who ranked fifth in the spring tournament:

00:21:07.770 --> 00:21:09.250
Ueshige Suzu.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:12.560
Himematsu High School 
(South Osaka)
 2nd Year
 Ueshige Suzu

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:10.900
Last year she was the fourth player,

00:21:10.900 --> 00:21:13.040
but this year she'll be playing first!

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:17.290
Lastly, representing Nagano, 
we have Kiyosumi High School's

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:19.750
Kiyosumi High School 
(Nagano)
 1st Year
 Kataoka Yuuki

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:19.790
Kataoka Yuuki.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:23.170
Huh? A cape?!

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:25.800
Is that what she bought the other day?

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:27.300
Miss Kataoka!

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:29.220
A word before the match?

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.890
Are you nervous?

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.060
<i>Here they are!</i>

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:36.270
Sorry, we're short on time, 
so we'll pass for today.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:37.270
Come this way.

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:39.210
You idiot.

00:21:39.210 --> 00:21:41.640
If it's not Kiyosumi's Haramura, 
you don't need to talk to them!

00:21:41.640 --> 00:21:44.190
But the memo said to 
keep an eye on Kiyosumi!

00:21:44.580 --> 00:21:47.950
The whole Nagano prefecture has 
probably dropped in level, anyway.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:50.920
<i>I feel like...</i>

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:57.730
<i>they're ridiculing every single one of us.</i>

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:14.350
<i>I'll show them whether our 
prefecture is weak or not!</i>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next time</b>

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>East Wind</b>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:38.060
These crepes all look really delicious!

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:39.180
It's hard to decide.

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:41.310
They all look so good, you can't choose.

00:23:41.310 --> 00:23:43.630
At times like that, this is the way to go!

00:23:43.630 --> 00:23:45.650
You can't go wrong when you choose tacos!

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:48.030
I guess they do look a little similar...

00:23:49.940 --> 00:23:55.250
<b>Watch Again!</b>
